{
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Gather your transaction evidence",
      "detail": "Collect your original invoice for Rs. 25,000, your return pickup receipt showing you returned the defective mobile phone on 10 September 2026, and the copies of your emails with ShopKart's customer support. Check if your invoice mentions a specific refund period, as refusing a refund after receiving returned defective goods is listed as an unfair trade practice [SRC:CPA2019-S2-47-viii]. Under e-commerce rules, marketplace sellers must not refuse to refund money when defective goods are returned [SRC:ECOM2020-R6-3]."
    },
    {
      "title": "Send a formal written complaint to ShopKart's Grievance Officer",
      "detail": "Since more than 30 days have passed without your refund, write directly to ShopKart's Grievance Officer. E-commerce platforms are required to appoint a Grievance Officer whose details must be displayed on their platform [SRC:ECOM2020-R4-4]. State that you are seeking a full refund of Rs. 25,000 for the defective phone you returned on 10 September 2026. By law, the Grievance Officer must acknowledge your complaint within 48 hours and resolve it within one month of receipt [SRC:ECOM2020-R4-5]. If you bought the phone from a third-party seller on ShopKart, you may also request the seller's details in writing from the platform [SRC:ECOM2020-R5-3-a]."
    },
    {
      "title": "Register a grievance with the National Consumer Helpline",
      "detail": "If ShopKart's Grievance Officer does not resolve your issue, file a consumer grievance with the National Consumer Helpline. You can call them on toll-free 1915 or 1800114000 (8 AM to 8 PM), send a WhatsApp message to +918800001915, or register online at consumerhelpline.gov.in [SRC:NCH-CONTACT]."
    },
    {
      "title": "File a consumer complaint electronically on e-Jagriti",
      "detail": "If the dispute remains unresolved, you may consider filing a formal consumer complaint with the District Consumer Commission [SRC:CPA2019-S35-1]. You can file online through e-jagriti.gov.in [SRC:CPA2019-S35-1]. Because your claim is Rs. 25,000 (which is up to Rs. 5 lakh), the filing fee is Nil [SRC:CDRC2023-R7-FEE]. Make sure to file within two years from when the cause of action arose [SRC:CPA2019-S69]. The Commission has the power to order remedies such as a full refund with interest and compensation [SRC:CPA2019-S39-1], and may also direct parties to consider mediation if a settlement appears possible [SRC:CPA2019-S37-1]."
    }
  ]
}

